# Winning a fight started from narration hands the scene back, with the body in it.
#
# The other half of "does victory end the fight phase". A narration fight returns through
# NarrativeController.OnFightCompleted rather than through travel: the enemy leaves play, a corpse is
# spawned into the area, and a fresh narration segment opens on it. Reaching LocationInteraction is
# only the first half of that — a run that came back to a scene still holding a live enemy would pass
# a mode check and be wrong, so the corpse is asserted too.
#
# The fight is entered by the attack verb (see cli/verb/attack/success.cli for the flag reasoning).
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Hall" --period dawn --observe-only brewer

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
goal attack
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

wait mode Fighting 90
fight-end victory

# Back in the scene, and the fight really is over — not merely off screen.
wait mode LocationInteraction 90
advance 12 180

# The victory's own consequence: the enemy is out of play and their body is in the area. This is
# what tells a returned scene apart from an abandoned one.
inspect pois
expect-state pois Corpse

quit
